{title: 292 - Jesus, I Come}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #292 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 292}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Out of my bondage, sorrow and night,
[C/G]Jesus, [G]I come, Jesus, [F#dim]I [D]come;
[D/F#]Into [G]Thy freedom, gladness and light,
[G]Jesus, I come [C/G]to [G]Thee;
[G]Out of my sickness into [F#dim]Thy [G]health,
[G]Out of my want [C/G]and into [G]Thy wealth,
[G]Out of my [F#dim]sin and [D]into Thyself,
[D/A]Jesus, [Em]I come [D/F#]to [D7/F#]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Out of my shameful failure and loss,
[C/G]Jesus, [G]I come, Jesus, [F#dim]I [D]come;
[D/F#]Into [G]the glorious gain of Thy cross,
[G]Jesus, I come [C/G]to [G]Thee;
[G]Out of earth's sorrows into [F#dim]Thy [G]balm,
[G]Out of life's storms [C/G]and into [G]Thy calm,
[G]Out of distress [F#dim]to [D]jubilant psalm,
[D/A]Jesus, [Em]I come [D/F#]to [D7/F#]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Out of unrest and arrogant pride,
[C/G]Jesus, [G]I come, Jesus, [F#dim]I [D]come;
[D/F#]Into [G]Thy blessed will to abide,
[G]Jesus, I come [C/G]to [G]Thee;
[G]Out of myself to dwell [F#dim]in Thy [G]love,
[G]Out of despair into [C/G]raptures [G]above,
[G]Upward for [F#dim]aye on [D]wings like a dove,
[D/A]Jesus, [Em]I come [D/F#]to [D7/F#]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Out of the fear and dread of the tomb,
[C/G]Jesus, [G]I come, Jesus, [F#dim]I [D]come;
[D/F#]Into [G]the joy and light of Thy home,
[G]Jesus, I come [C/G]to [G]Thee;
[G]Out of the depths of ruin [F#dim]untold,
[G]Into the peace of [C/G]Thy sheltering [G]fold,
[G]Ever Thy [F#dim]glorious [D]face to behold,
[D/A]Jesus, [Em]I come [D/F#]to [D7/F#]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
